  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d822886221c0364b9fc056e41f01c23, type: 3}
  m_Name: 8_AutomationSurface
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Tutorial
  ID: 7
  Message:
  - 'Automation allows you to automate the production of resources instead of manually
    picking and dropping resources from one machine to other '
  - You can enter the automation mode by pressing the <b>AUTO</b> button on the top
    right of the screen. Once the button turns yellow then you are in automation
    mode. You can press the button again to exit automation mode.
  - Automation mode allows you to place conveyors from one machine's output node
    to other machine's input node.
  - Once in automation mode you will see a <color=green>green</color> and <color=red>red
    dot</color> on the placed machines. The <color=green>green dot</color> is the
    input node and the <color=red>red dot</color> is the output node.
  - To construct a conveyor drag from one machine's <color=red>red node (output)</color>
    to other machine's <color=green>green node (input)</color>. If the conveyor does
    not build that means that the first machine's output is not compatible with second
    machine's input
